  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy, showing that multiprofile aggregation is the dominant design lever (~13-point gain over single profile). The key remaining uncertainty within this promising regime is whether the aggregation strategy itself can be improved: does a transformer-based aggregation capture inter-profile relationships that a simple average pool misses? config_006 is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (only aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer), directly isolating the aggregation effect. This is the best use of the next experiment because: (1) it exploits the strongest evidence by testing a logical extension of the best configuration, (2) it reduces uncertainty about a design choice that will propagate into all future multimodal experiments, and (3) the answer—whether transformer helps, hurts, or is neutral—will determine whether to invest further in aggregation complexity or pivot to encoder exploration (scgpt) and multimodal fusion. No other single experiment provides as much information per trial at this stage."
}

